From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:18:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 066/117] input: touchscreen: apple_z2: add D111 support

The iPhone 7 Plus D111 touchscreen uses the same Apple Z2 driver family as
the existing devices, but its Gen2 firmware and runtime protocol are not
interchangeable with J172. D111 requires two regulator-controlled rails, a
longer boot window, 8-bit HBPP wire order, firmware-provided SPI timing,
four dynamic calibration payloads and direct runtime reports identified by
type 0x44.

Extend apple_z2 with a D111 match and keep the platform differences behind
the existing device instance. Add balanced HV/core/clock power sequencing,
a shared reset-pulse helper, D111 boot preambles and firmware-ready
handling. Parse the firmware configuration into per-device timing and DMA
limits, validate calibration provider, size and presence, and build the
D111 HBPP14 calibration packet with explicit byte order and checksums.

Short D111 transfers which must avoid the controller DMA path are made
full duplex at the individual transfer, preserving the wire length and
selecting the existing PIO path. This keeps the constraint at the consumer
transfer rather than changing the SPI controller for every child. Runtime
dispatch rejects packets unless the payload is long enough and carries
report type 0x44 before passing it to the touch parser; coordinates are
scaled from the validated surface descriptor.

Probe fails before input registration when required supplies or
calibration data are unavailable. Firmware, SPI and protocol failures flow
through the existing stop path, while power rollback tracks each enabled
regulator and clock so partial initialization and later shutdown remain
balanced. No input-core, SPI-core or global PMIC lookup is introduced.

The complete series built Image.gz, DTBs and modules. On D111, all four
live calibration blobs had the expected 1024, 992, 1474 and 208 byte
sizes; apple-z2 bound to spi0.0 and evtest recorded 1,382 events with 11
balanced touch sequences. The IRQ count increased by 186 without Z2, SPI,
regulator or Chestnut errors. This patch was checked with checkpatch.pl
--strict.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

